{"assessment":"The source supports the normalized-friction fits for the viscous-inertial transition. The public control St ranges from 0.01 to 300. The common fixed condition K_phi = J + 0.1 I^2 = 0.065 is a constructed slice through both source global fits, not two simulation runs from the two matched mu_f branches. The St=.65 and 206.5 points are provenance for how the reference slice was chosen, not paired direct samples. The derived relations J(St)=0.065/(1+0.1 St), K_mu(St)=0.065*(1+alpha_mu St)/(1+0.1 St), and r(St)=1+a_mu*sqrt(K_mu(St)) are consistent with the source equations and fits. The private branch mu_f=0.15 uses a_mu=14.3 and alpha_mu=0.029; the alternate branch mu_f=0.80 uses a_mu=26.5 and alpha_mu=0.00875. All constants are anchored. The case is authoring-ready.","case_authoring_ready":true,"claims":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":125,"line_start":125,"support":"Stokes number St is defined as the ratio of inertial to viscous stress scales I^2/J."},{"line_end":177,"line_start":177,"support":"inset provides mu/mu_c vs K_mu with a single fit mu = mu_c (1 + a_mu K_mu^{1/2}) with a_mu=14.3"},{"line_end":246,"line_start":246,"support":"K=K_phi=J+alpha_phi I^2, where alpha_phi=0.1"},{"line_end":252,"line_start":252,"support":"K_mu = J + alpha_mu I^2 with alpha_mu = 0.029"},{"line_end":276,"line_start":274,"support":"two simulation runs with the same K-value (K=0.065) at St=0.65 and 206.5"},{"line_end":358,"line_start":358,"support":"Table: mu_f=0.15, a_mu=14.3, alpha_mu=0.029"}],"applicability":"Valid for the reference interparticle friction mu_f=0.15 and for St in the range 0.01-300.","claim_id":"r_vs_St_muf015","control_domains":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":238,"line_start":238,"support":"The range of St numbers in this study is 0.01-300."}],"control_name":"St","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"The range of St numbers in this study is 0.01-300.","maximum":300.0,"minimum":0.01}],"control_names":["St"],"depends_on":[],"fixed_condition_ids":["K_phi_common","mu_f_reference"],"mechanism_ids":["viscous_inertial_rheology"],"oracle_outputs":{"r":{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"param":"a_mu_muf015"},{"args":[{"args":[{"args":[{"param":"K_phi_common"},{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"param":"alpha_mu_muf015"},{"var":"St"}],"op":"multiply"}],"op":"add"}],"op":"multiply"},{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"param":"alpha_phi"},{"var":"St"}],"op":"multiply"}],"op":"add"}],"op":"divide"},{"param":"half"}],"op":"power"}],"op":"multiply"}],"op":"add"}},"quantitative_form":"r(St) = 1 + 14.3 * sqrt(0.065 * (1 + 0.029 * St) / (1 + 0.1 * St))","readout_names":["r"],"statement":"For the reference interparticle friction mu_f=0.15, the normalized friction r = mu/mu_c as a function of Stokes number St is given by r(St) = 1 + a_mu * sqrt(K_mu(St)), where K_mu(St) = K_phi * (1 + alpha_mu * St) / (1 + 0.1 * St) with K_phi = 0.065, a_mu = 14.3, and alpha_mu = 0.029.","statistical_basis":"Central value implied by the reported fits at constructed K_phi=0.065; coefficients a_mu and alpha_mu from Table 1.","uncertainty":"mu_c has uncertainty ±0.02 with convention source_unspecified; no uncertainty reported for a_mu or alpha_mu; no pointwise uncertainty for the derived r(St) curve."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":125,"line_start":125,"support":"Stokes number St is defined as the ratio of inertial to viscous stress scales I^2/J."},{"line_end":246,"line_start":246,"support":"K=K_phi=J+alpha_phi I^2, where alpha_phi=0.1"},{"line_end":276,"line_start":274,"support":"two simulation runs with the same K-value (K=0.065) at St=0.65 and 206.5"},{"line_end":375,"line_start":340,"support":"Figure 6 caption and surrounding text: mu/mu_c versus K_mu with fit mu = mu_c(1 + a_mu K_mu^{1/2}) for changed friction; curves collapse against K_mu with alpha_mu decreasing with increasing mu_f."},{"line_end":360,"line_start":360,"support":"Table: mu_f=0.80, a_mu=26.5, alpha_mu=0.00875"}],"applicability":"Valid for the alternate interparticle friction mu_f=0.80 and for St in the range 0.01-300.","claim_id":"r_vs_St_muf080","control_domains":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":238,"line_start":238,"support":"The range of St numbers in this study is 0.01-300."}],"control_name":"St","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"The range of St numbers in this study is 0.01-300.","maximum":300.0,"minimum":0.01}],"control_names":["St"],"depends_on":[],"fixed_condition_ids":["K_phi_common","mu_f_alternate"],"mechanism_ids":["viscous_inertial_rheology"],"oracle_outputs":{"r":{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"param":"a_mu_muf080"},{"args":[{"args":[{"args":[{"param":"K_phi_common"},{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"param":"alpha_mu_muf080"},{"var":"St"}],"op":"multiply"}],"op":"add"}],"op":"multiply"},{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"param":"alpha_phi"},{"var":"St"}],"op":"multiply"}],"op":"add"}],"op":"divide"},{"param":"half"}],"op":"power"}],"op":"multiply"}],"op":"add"}},"quantitative_form":"r(St) = 1 + 26.5 * sqrt(0.065 * (1 + 0.00875 * St) / (1 + 0.1 * St))","readout_names":["r"],"statement":"For the alternate interparticle friction mu_f=0.80, the normalized friction r = mu/mu_c as a function of Stokes number St is given by r(St) = 1 + a_mu * sqrt(K_mu(St)), where K_mu(St) = K_phi * (1 + alpha_mu * St) / (1 + 0.1 * St) with K_phi = 0.065, a_mu = 26.5, and alpha_mu = 0.00875.","statistical_basis":"Central value implied by the reported fits at constructed K_phi=0.065; coefficients a_mu and alpha_mu from Table 1.","uncertainty":"mu_c has uncertainty ±0.08 with convention source_unspecified; no uncertainty reported for a_mu or alpha_mu; no pointwise uncertainty for the derived r(St) curve."}],"controls":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":125,"line_start":125,"support":"The Stokes number St is defined as the ratio of inertial to viscous stress scales I^2/J."},{"line_end":238,"line_start":238,"support":"The range of St numbers in this study is 0.01-300."}],"definition":"Stokes number, defined as the ratio of inertial to viscous stress scales I^2/J.","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"The range of St numbers in this study is 0.01-300.","maximum":300.0,"minimum":0.01,"name":"St","unit":"dimensionless"}],"fixed_conditions":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":246,"line_start":246,"support":"K=K_phi=J+alpha_phi I^2, where alpha_phi=0.1"},{"line_end":276,"line_start":274,"support":"two simulation runs with the same K-value (K=0.065) at St=0.65 and 206.5"},{"line_end":372,"line_start":340,"support":"Figure 6 caption and discussion of changed friction fits; Table 1 lists coefficients for mu_f=0.15, 0.5, 0.8"}],"condition_id":"K_phi_common","statement":"For both private mu_f branches, the Oracle evaluates the source-reported K_phi/K_mu fit laws on the constructed slice K_phi=J+0.1 I^2=0.065; the source directly reports this K_phi at St=0.65 and 206.5 in the reference analysis."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":193,"line_start":193,"support":"mu_f=0.15 (which is our reference mu_f)"}],"condition_id":"mu_f_reference","statement":"The reference interparticle friction coefficient is mu_f = 0.15."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":360,"line_start":360,"support":"Table: mu_f=0.80"}],"condition_id":"mu_f_alternate","statement":"An alternate interparticle friction coefficient is mu_f = 0.80."}],"mechanisms":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":123,"line_start":123,"support":"K = J + alpha I^2 with alpha = 1/St_{v->i}"},{"line_end":125,"line_start":125,"support":"Stokes number St is defined as the ratio of inertial to viscous stress scales I^2/J"},{"line_end":177,"line_start":177,"support":"Fits mu = mu_c(1 + a_mu K_mu^{1/2}) with a_mu=14.3"},{"line_end":252,"line_start":246,"support":"Definitions of K_phi and K_mu with alpha_phi=0.1 and alpha_mu=0.029"},{"line_end":360,"line_start":358,"support":"Table of fit coefficients for mu_f=0.15, 0.5, 0.8"}],"equations":["K_phi = J + alpha_phi I^2, alpha_phi = 0.1","K_mu = J + alpha_mu I^2","r = mu/mu_c = 1 + a_mu * sqrt(K_mu)","phi = phi_c (1 - a_phi sqrt(K_phi))"],"mechanism_id":"viscous_inertial_rheology","parameters":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":246,"line_start":246,"support":"K=K_phi=J+alpha_phi I^2, where alpha_phi=1/St_{v->i}=0.1"}],"name":"alpha_phi","role":"coefficient in K_phi definition","uncertainty":"none reported","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.1},{"anchors":[{"line_end":177,"line_start":177,"support":"inset provides mu/mu_c vs K_mu with a single fit mu = mu_c (1 + a_mu K_mu^{1/2}) with a_mu=14.3"},{"line_end":358,"line_start":358,"support":"Table: mu_f=0.15, a_mu=14.3"}],"name":"a_mu_muf015","role":"fit coefficient in r = 1 + a_mu sqrt(K_mu) for mu_f=0.15","uncertainty":"none reported","unit":"dimensionless","value":14.3},{"anchors":[{"line_end":252,"line_start":252,"support":"K_mu = J + alpha_mu I^2 with alpha_mu = 0.029"},{"line_end":358,"line_start":358,"support":"Table: mu_f=0.15, alpha_mu=0.029"}],"name":"alpha_mu_muf015","role":"coefficient in K_mu for mu_f=0.15","uncertainty":"none reported","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.029},{"anchors":[{"line_end":360,"line_start":360,"support":"Table: mu_f=0.80, a_mu=26.5"}],"name":"a_mu_muf080","role":"fit coefficient in r = 1 + a_mu sqrt(K_mu) for mu_f=0.80","uncertainty":"none reported","unit":"dimensionless","value":26.5},{"anchors":[{"line_end":360,"line_start":360,"support":"Table: mu_f=0.80, alpha_mu=0.00875"}],"name":"alpha_mu_muf080","role":"coefficient in K_mu for mu_f=0.80","uncertainty":"none reported","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.00875},{"anchors":[{"line_end":248,"line_start":248,"support":"mu_c = 0.30 ± 0.02 at jamming"},{"line_end":360,"line_start":358,"support":"Table: mu_c values for different mu_f"}],"name":"mu_c","role":"critical macroscopic friction at jamming","uncertainty":"±0.02 for mu_f=0.15, ±0.05 for mu_f=0.5, ±0.08 for mu_f=0.8; convention source_unspecified","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.3},{"anchors":[{"line_end":177,"line_start":177,"support":"mu = mu_c (1 + a_mu K_mu^{1/2})"}],"name":"one","role":"additive constant in r = 1 + a_mu sqrt(K_mu)","uncertainty":"none","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.0},{"anchors":[{"line_end":177,"line_start":177,"support":"mu = mu_c (1 + a_mu K_mu^{1/2})"}],"name":"half","role":"exponent in sqrt(K_mu)","uncertainty":"none","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.5},{"anchors":[{"line_end":246,"line_start":246,"support":"K=K_phi=J+alpha_phi I^2, where alpha_phi=0.1"},{"line_end":276,"line_start":274,"support":"two simulation runs with the same K-value (K=0.065) at St=0.65 and 206.5"},{"line_end":372,"line_start":340,"support":"Figure 6 caption and discussion of changed friction fits; Table 1 lists coefficients for mu_f=0.15, 0.5, 0.8"}],"name":"K_phi_common","role":"constructed slice through both source global fits: K_phi = J + 0.1 I^2 = 0.065","uncertainty":"none reported","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.065}],"statement":"The macroscopic friction coefficient mu is governed by a single dimensionless number K_mu = J + alpha_mu I^2, with alpha_mu = 1/St_{v->i}^mu, and the normalized friction r = mu/mu_c follows r = 1 + a_mu * sqrt(K_mu). The packing fraction phi follows phi = phi_c (1 - a_phi sqrt(K_phi)) with K_phi = J + alpha_phi I^2 and alpha_phi = 0.1.","variable_names":["St","J","I","K_phi","K_mu","mu","mu_c","r","a_mu","alpha_mu","phi","phi_c","a_phi","alpha_phi"]}],"paper_scope":"Particle-resolved simulations of dense frictional suspensions undergoing the viscous-inertial transition using pressure-imposed rheology. The study varies fluid viscosity, shear rate, and granular pressure, and examines the effect of interparticle friction on the transition. The key findings are the distinct scalings of packing fraction phi and macroscopic friction mu, governed by different alpha values, and the role of tangential contact and lubrication forces.","readouts":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":177,"line_start":177,"support":"mu/mu_c vs K_mu with fit mu = mu_c (1 + a_mu K_mu^{1/2})"},{"line_end":248,"line_start":248,"support":"mu_c = 0.30 ± 0.02 at jamming"},{"line_end":276,"line_start":274,"support":"two simulation runs with the same K-value (K=0.065) at St=0.65 and 206.5"},{"line_end":372,"line_start":340,"support":"Figure 6 caption and discussion of changed friction fits; Table 1 lists coefficients for mu_f=0.15, 0.5, 0.8"}],"definition":"Normalized macroscopic friction coefficient, r = mu/mu_c.","name":"r","resolution":null,"statistic":"Central value implied by the reported fits at constructed K_phi=0.065; not a table of raw means at every St and mu_f.","uncertainty":"mu_c has uncertainty ±0.02 for mu_f=0.15, ±0.05 for mu_f=0.5, ±0.08 for mu_f=0.8, with convention source_unspecified; no uncertainty reported for a_mu or alpha_mu; no pointwise uncertainty for the derived r(St) curve.","unit":"dimensionless"}],"source":{"arxiv_versioned_id":"2505.04242v1","citation":"Sudarshan Konidena, Tangential Forces Govern the Viscous-Inertial Transition in Dense Frictional Suspensions, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/66pp-4rdj","journal_doi":"10.1103/66pp-4rdj"},"source_ambiguities":[]}
